+# TARGET: Rhythm Heaven (US) → macOS / Windows / iOS
+
+Added 2026-10-09. Everything above still governs. This section records
+what is specific to the Rhythm Heaven effort and what the first survey
+found. Plan: `docs/rhythm-heaven-plan.md`.
+
+## Status of the gate
+
+The FIRMWARE-MENU GATE above was passed by the framework (PLAN.md
+Phases 2–6, gates G1/G2/G3). It is **not** being re-earned for this
+title, but it is the regression floor: every portability change must
+keep G1 (firmware traversal vs fresh `ndsref`) green. Game work is
+allowed; ARM-interpreter-on-hot-path, BIOS-SWI stubs, edits to
+`generated/**`, and load-bearing HLE are still forbidden.
+
+`AGENTS.md` is a standing user policy: no perf/validation matrices, no
+multi-route/multi-repetition benchmark legs. Gameplay validation is
+capped at **one** run per kind unless the user asks for more.
+
+## The ROM
+
+`3588 - Rhythm Heaven (US)(XenoPhobia).nds` (repo root, untracked, 128 MiB
+image, SHA-1 `601b92b1603f1822543e264df55ab4152ded356c`).
+
+| field | value |
+|---|---|
+| title / code | `RHYTHMHEAVEN` / `YLZE`, maker `01`, rev 0, NDS (unit 0, not DSi-enhanced) |
+| ARM9 | ROM `0x4000`, load/entry `0x02000000` / `0x02000800`, `0x53B98` B (~339 KB) |
+| ARM7 | ROM `0x15D400`, load/entry `0x02380000`, `0x26F28` B; no ARM7 overlays |
+| ARM9 overlays | table `0x57C00`, **165 overlays**, all uncompressed, ~1 MB total, max `0xAB20` B |
+| overlay RAM slots | only **3 load addresses**: `0x0228FA60` (105 ovl), `0x02287660` (59), `0x0227CB20` (1) |
+| FNT / FAT | `0x184400` / `0x18C400` |
+| secure area | stored **decrypted**; runner re-encrypts to card form (`runner/src/io.cpp` ~229) |
+| save type | **unknown** — not in the header. Determine (melonDS game DB / observed AUXSPI traffic) and declare in `[cartridge]`; do not rely on the 8 KiB EEPROM default |
+
+Consequences:
+
+- Overlays are plain bytes in the ROM, so they can be recompiled **ahead
+  of time from the ROM file** instead of only from RAM captures. But
+  165 bodies share 3 addresses: banks must be content-validated and
+  keyed by bytes/bank identity, never bare PC (see
+  `docs/overlay-strategy.md`, `HLE_ARCHITECTURE.md` wrapper rule).
+- The code footprint is small next to SM64DS (1.3 GiB of C), so full
+  static coverage with Tier 3 idle is the target, not an aspiration.
+  That is also what makes the iOS port viable.
+- It is a stylus + audio-timing game. Touch, SPU exactness and
+  input→audio/video latency matter more than raw throughput.
+
+## Repository shape
+
+This repo is the **framework**. Per-title work lives in a separate
+title repo (siblings so far: `supermario64dsrecomp`, MarioKartDSRecomp;
+neither is checked out here). Rhythm Heaven needs its own
+(`rhythmheavenrecomp`, at `~/dev/rhythmheavenrecomp`, outside iCloud Drive): config TOMLs, bank-capture tools, generated
+banks (ignored), `game.toml`. It is wired in with
+`-DNDS_TITLE_BANK_DIR=<dir> -DNDS_TITLE_ROM_SHA1=601b92b1…`. Do not put
+title names or addresses into the shared runner.
+
+Framework changes needed by the port (portability, new recompiler
+features, bus/device fixes) go in **this** repo; ROM-specific config,
+overlay manifests and `[display]/[cartridge]` settings go in the title repo.
+
+## Environment facts (surveyed 2026-10-09)
+
+- Machine: Apple M3 (arm64), 16 GB, AppleClang 21, CMake 4.4, Ninja,
+  Xcode present. SDL3 and libslirp not confirmed installed.
+- **Recompiler** builds on macOS arm64 from a clean tree
+  (`cmake -G Ninja -B <build> recompiler`) and its decode/cycle/HLE
+  tests pass, including the three that take `<nds_recompile> <work-dir>`
+  args (run by `tools/rh_suite.py`).
+- **Runner** has not been built on macOS. Known Windows/mingw
+  assumptions: `host_unwind_x64.cpp` + `host_profile.cpp` (PE
+  `.pdata` unwinding), `live_overlay*.cpp` (bundled TCC, shared
+  library suffix, process spawn), `wifi_net.cpp` sockets, a hardcoded
+  `F:/Projects/recomp-ui` default in `runner/CMakeLists.txt`, PGO tied
+  to mingw-gcc, `.ps1`-only helper scripts under `tools/`.
+- **Dumps are missing**: `bios/` has only the `.toml` configs. The
+  faithful path needs `biosnds7.rom`, `biosnds9.rom`, `firmware.bin`
+  (hashes in README). Without them only the opt-in FreeBIOS path
+  (`--freebios --generated-firmware --boot direct`) can run. That path
+  is not the oracle-diffed floor; the retail dumps stay authoritative.
+- **melonDS.app** (v1.1, universal) in the repo root is a GUI emulator
+  for eyeballing and for finding the save type. It is **not** the
+  oracle: the oracle is `ndsref`, melonDS pinned to `1.0rc` plus the
+  TCP patch, built by `oracle/setup-melonds.sh` into `third_party/`
+  (gitignored). It has not been built on macOS yet.
+- The repo sits under iCloud Drive. Keep build trees, `generated/`
+  and title bank output **outside** iCloud (hundreds of MB of C and
+  thousands of object files will thrash sync).
+
+## Port constraints to keep in view
+
+- **No generated banks, ROMs, BIOS or firmware in any distributed
+  artifact.** Banks are derived from Nintendo code, so every platform's
+  deliverable is "build/run with your own ROM (and BIOS)": a local
+  regen+build pipeline, not a prebuilt binary containing the game.
+- **iOS forbids runtime codegen.** Tier 2 / live-overlay (TCC + shared
+  library) cannot exist there, and the Tier-3 interpreter must be
+  idle in normal play. All Rhythm Heaven code reachable in play must
+  be in static banks. Because banks are ROM-derived, an iOS build is a
+  user-built/self-signed app, not an App Store binary.
+- **GPL-3.0-or-later**: `nds_runner` links vendored melonDS code
+  (Wi-Fi, GPU3D). Distribution must ship source and `LICENSE-GPL`;
+  App Store terms are generally incompatible with this.
+- **Renderer**: the compute backend needs OpenGL 4.3. macOS tops out
+  at 4.1 and iOS has no desktop GL, so Apple platforms use the
+  threaded software renderer (`NDS_3D_RENDERER=soft`) unless a Metal
+  backend is written. Software is the accuracy floor anyway.
+- **Known fidelity gaps that a 2D-heavy title may hit** (PLAN.md WS-D):
+  2D windows (Win0/Win1/OBJ window/WINOUT) unimplemented, main-memory
+  display FIFO absent, SPU capture bits inert, cartridge chip type
+  fixed to EEPROM unless configured. Close these as the oracle diff
+  reaches them; do not pre-build blind.
+
+## Decisions and tooling (2026-10-09)
+
+- **BIOS**: no retail dumps are available; bring-up uses the FreeBIOS path
+  (`third_party/freebios`). It is not melonDS's built-in replacement, so
+  an oracle diff needs `ndsref` to load the same binaries (unverified).
+- **iOS** means a user-built, self-signed app; no prebuilt binaries on any
+  platform. The deliverable is a *builder* that turns the user's ROM into
+  `.exe` / `.app` / `.ipa` (`.ipa` only buildable on a Mac with Xcode).
+- **Windows** is verified by the user running `tools/rh_suite.py` and
+  returning `build-suite/report.json`. The suite checks artifacts and
+  builds only; no gameplay, no benchmarks (AGENTS.md). First macOS run:
+  34 pass / 0 fail / 4 warn. All 165 overlays + ARM9 + ARM7 decode with
+  zero codegen gaps; coverage (indirect targets) is still Phase 3 work.
+- Rerun the suite after any recompiler or portability change:
+  `python tools/rh_suite.py --rom <rom> --work <dir outside iCloud>`.
